.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt READAHEAD 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm readahead ,
.Nm posix_fadvise
.Nd advise the kernel of reads to come
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In fcntl.h
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn readahead "int fd" "off_t offset" "size_t count"
.Ft int
.Fn posix_fadvise "int fd" "off_t offset" "off_t len" "int advice"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The page cache fills a page when a read first asks for it and keeps one
policy for every file, so neither call changes what the kernel does.
.Fn readahead
checks
.Fa fd
and returns 0, as Linux does once it has queued the reads.
.Fn posix_fadvise
checks
.Fa fd ,
.Fa len
and
.Fa advice ,
which is one of
.Dv POSIX_FADV_NORMAL ,
.Dv POSIX_FADV_RANDOM ,
.Dv POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL ,
.Dv POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED ,
.Dv POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED
and
.Dv POSIX_FADV_NOREUSE ,
and returns 0.
.Pp
The i386 system call numbers are 225 for
.Fn readahead ,
250 for
.Fn fadvise64 ,
which takes a 32-bit length, and 272 for
.Fn fadvise64_64 ,
which takes a 64-bit length and is the one musl calls for
.Fn posix_fadvise .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
0, or for
.Fn readahead
-1 with
.Va errno
set; musl's
.Fn posix_fadvise
returns the error number itself.
.Sh EXAMPLES
GNU
.Xr cp 1 ,
.Xr cat 1
and
.Xr sort 1
call
.Fn posix_fadvise
on what they read, and BusyBox's
.Xr readahead 1
calls
.Fn readahead
on each file it names.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[ESPIPE]"
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa fd
is not open, was opened with
.Dv O_PATH ,
or for
.Fn readahead
is not open for reading.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
For
.Fn readahead ,
.Fa fd
is not a regular file; for
.Fn posix_fadvise ,
.Fa len
is negative or
.Fa advice
is none of the six.
.It Bq Er ESPIPE
For
.Fn posix_fadvise ,
.Fa fd
is a pipe or a FIFO.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr read 2
